---
export const prerender = true;
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const effectiveDate = 'July 29, 2026';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy | Chord Sequence"
  description="Chord Sequence privacy policy — what an account involves, what we store when you save a song, and how sharing works."
  canonicalUrl="https://chordsequence.com/privacy/"
>
  <main class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 sm:px-6 py-16 sm:py-24">
    <nav class="flex items-center gap-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground mb-10">
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-foreground transition-colors">Home</a>
      <svg class="h-3.5 w-3.5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"><path d="m9 18 6-6-6-6"/></svg>
      <span class="text-foreground">Privacy Policy</span>
    </nav>

    <header class="mb-12">
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold text-foreground tracking-tight mb-4">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="text-sm text-muted-foreground">Effective date: {effectiveDate}</p>
    </header>

    <div class="space-y-10 text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">The short version</h2>
        <p>
          Chord Sequence works without an account. You can build chord progressions, play them, transpose them and
          export audio without giving us anything at all. Saving is the exception: to keep a song in a library that
          follows you between devices you create a free account with an email address and a password, and the songs
          you save are stored on our servers. They stay private to you unless you choose to share one. We also use
          Google Analytics to see how the site is used.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">What data is stored — and where</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">Some of it never leaves your device. The app keeps the following <strong class="text-foreground">in your browser</strong>, using the Web Storage API (<code class="text-primary text-sm">localStorage</code>):</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-sm">
          <li>Your work in the bass and guitar tab editors, saved as you type</li>
          <li>A draft of the chord progression you are editing, so it survives a reload</li>
          <li>App preferences — metronome settings, custom rhythm styles, how you like chord names written, whether you have seen the intro</li>
          <li>Your login session token, if you are signed in</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3 mb-3">
          We have no access to any of that, and clearing your browser's site data erases it.
        </p>
        <p class="mb-3">The rest is stored <strong class="text-foreground">on our servers</strong>, and only if you create an account:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-sm">
          <li>Your email address and a securely hashed password</li>
          <li>The songs you save — title, chords, tempo, sections and playback settings</li>
          <li>Custom rhythm styles you have saved to your account</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">
          This is held in Supabase, the database service behind the app. Saved songs are private to your account
          unless you share one.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">Accounts and saved songs</h2>
        <p>
          Creating an account is optional — every tool on the site works without one. You need one only to save a song
          to a library that follows you between devices. Saved songs are private to your account by default: the Share
          button makes a single song readable by anyone holding its link, and you can switch that off again at any
          time. To have your account and everything in it deleted, contact us at the address below.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">External requests</h2>
        <p class="mb-3">The app loads the following third-party services:</p>
        <ul class="list-disc list-inside space-y-1 text-sm">
          <li>
            <strong class="text-foreground">Google Fonts</strong> — to load the Inter, Lora, and Space Mono typefaces
            from <code class="text-primary text-sm">fonts.googleapis.com</code> and <code class="text-primary text-sm">fonts.gstatic.com</code>.
            Google may log your IP address and browser type when these fonts are requested.
            This request does not set any tracking cookies and is not used for advertising.
            See <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">Google's Privacy Policy</a> for details.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-foreground">Google Analytics</strong> — to measure how the site is used: pages viewed,
            which tools get opened, roughly where visitors come from. It sets cookies (see below) and Google processes
            the data under its own <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>.
            We use it to decide what to build next, not to identify anyone.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong class="text-foreground">Supabase</strong> — the database and sign-in service. It is contacted when
            you create an account, sign in, or save, load or share a song. See
            <a href="https://supabase.com/privacy" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">Supabase's Privacy Policy</a>.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="mt-3">No advertising pixels or ad networks are loaded by this site, and we do not sell or share your data with anyone.</p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">Hosting and server logs</h2>
        <p>
          Chord Sequence is hosted on Netlify. Netlify may collect standard server access logs (IP address, browser,
          pages visited, timestamp) as part of normal web hosting operations. This data is processed by Netlify under
          their own <a href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="text-primary hover:underline">Privacy Policy</a>.
          We do not access individual server logs for tracking or profiling purposes.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">Cookies</h2>
        <p>
          Google Analytics sets cookies (named <code class="text-primary text-sm">_ga</code> and
          <code class="text-primary text-sm">_ga_*</code>) to tell repeat visits apart from new ones. We set none of
          our own: everything else the app remembers — your session, your drafts, your preferences — lives in
          <code class="text-primary text-sm">localStorage</code>, not in cookies.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">Children's privacy</h2>
        <p>
          The tools themselves can be used by anyone at any age — without an account we hold nothing about you.
          Accounts are a different matter: they are not intended for children under 16, since creating one means
          giving us an email address. We do not knowingly collect personal information from children, and if you
          believe a child has created an account, write to us and we will delete it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">Your rights over your data</h2>
        <p>
          If you have an account, you can ask us at any time for a copy of what we hold about you, for a correction,
          or for the whole lot to be deleted — account, saved songs and settings. Write to the address below and we
          will do it. You do not need a reason. If you use Chord Sequence without an account there is nothing to
          request: we hold nothing that identifies you.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p>
          If we make changes to this privacy policy, we will update the effective date at the top of this page.
          If the change is a material one and you have an account, we will also let you know by email. If you use
          the site without an account we have no way to reach you, so check back here if you have concerns.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section>
        <h2 class="text-xl font-bold text-foreground mb-3">Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions about this privacy policy? Reach us at <a href="/contact/" class="text-primary hover:underline">our contact page</a> or by email at
          <a href="mailto:corsinoelias@gmail.com" class="text-primary hover:underline">corsinoelias@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
      </section>

    </div>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
